  "question": {
    "text": "A microscope is having objective of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and eyepiece of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If tube length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and image is formed at the least distance of distinct vision, what is the magnification produced by the microscope. (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
